rows.en:
...This is a dream{f:.|.}
That's right{f:,|,} it has to be a dream{f:.|.}
This is a nightmare{f:!|!}
{f:Please|Please}!
If this is a dream, let me wake up{f:|}..................!{p}

"Good work, everyone!"
The last one went home.
All right, now the real thing begins{f:.|.}
I've come this far and made up my mind, so {f:I'm|I'm} going to settle once and for all whether Kazama really is an alien or just a nutcase{f:!|!}
I'm angry at Kazama's attitude, and if he's been acting like that half as a joke, {f:I|I} intend to make him apologize{f:.|.}
Except if he turns out to be a real alien, or a real nutcase, that is.
{f:I'm|I'm} convinced he's a nutcase, though.
No, he definitely is{f:.|.}{p}

I doubt it{f:,|,} but he won't suddenly go berserk, will he{f:?|?}
Either way, if it looks like we can't understand each other by talking, {f:I|I} plan to get out of here{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} decided to keep the conversation going without provoking him.
If I suddenly went straight to the heart of it, whether Kazama is an alien or not, that would be scary{f:.|.}{p}

What? Nobody told me it had come to that{f:!|!}
{f:No|No}, Kazama is completely off in another world{f:.|.}
"Oh, it was so long ago that I totally forgot{f:.|.} {f:Sorry, sorry|I'm so sorry}."
{f:I|I} played along nicely.{p}

"Whoa there!"
Kazama dodged {f:my punch|my attack} with quick footwork.
Thank goodness.
If he hadn't dodged, {f:I'd have punched Kazama with everything I had|by now I'd have... Kazama...}.
Even if {f:I|I} was the one who did it, that was a little reckless of me{f:.|.}
Everyone was startled too, frozen where they stood.{p}

"There, everyone's gone.
Let's hurry and start our briefing! Comrade!"
Kazama pulled {f:me|me} up and said it, gripping {f:my|my} hand tightly.
I thought it no longer mattered whether Kazama was really an alien or just a nutcase.
Wait{f: a minute| a second}, if I think about it, it does matter{f:.|.}
Either way, that means Kazama is extremely dangerous{f:!|!}
That's right{f:,|,} just being near him is dangerous, so why did {f:I|I} go and swing at him{f:?|?}
Just remembering it now gives me chills{f:.|.}
From here on, the way {f:I|I} should act toward him is...{p}

The door suddenly slammed shut.
It missed {f:my|my} nose by a hair.
If it had shut a moment later, the door might have hit {f:me|me} square on the head.{p}

"Shall we switch to our native tongue soon? The door to this room's been shut, too, after all. It's been a while, though, so I wonder if I can still speak it well."
{f:I|I} tried saying something like that, just in case.
It's all or nothing now, so maybe I should just go all the way and play the part of a Sunbararian{f:.|.}
Then, when I find an opening, I can run for it.
There's no need to put myself in danger right now{f:.|.}{p}

"No, there's no need to switch to our native tongue yet. For now, I'm still Nozomu Kazama, the Earthling, after all."
Kazama said.
Phew, {f:that's the right answer|that's just what I wanted to hear}, Kazama.{p}

"But don't worry. I'll get your memories back for you."
With that, Kazama looked at {f:me|me}.
Then he came walking toward {f:me|me}.
Now all I could see in front of me was Kazama's face.
What on earth is he going to do{f:?|?}
As I looked into his eyes, I gradually began to feel good.
It was a feeling like I was floating in water{f:.|.}
Kazama put his hand on {f:my|my} forehead and said,
"Now, relax. Try closing your eyes."{p}

And so {f:I|I} slowly closed my eyes.
And {f:what do you know|what do you know}, behind {f:my|my} eyelids I saw myself, living as a Sunbararian{f:!|!}
So this is a Sunbararian{f:...|...}
Why did I know that the alien shown there was {f:me|me}{f:?|?}
It looked completely different from a human.
Somehow, I couldn't help feeling that it was.{p}

My eyelids are heavy.
I feel like my eyes are about to close{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} had almost done what he told me, and I shook my head hard.
If I do what he says here, there's no telling what he'll do to me.
But I feel so good{f:.|.}
Fighting back my drooping eyelids, I barely managed to keep my eyes half open.{p}

{p}And {f:what do you know|what do you know}, a dazzling light like an aura burst out of {f:my|my} body{f:!|!}
"Gyaah☆"
The thing let out a short scream and pulled its tentacles off {f:my|my} body.
When I came to my senses, the light was gone from my body.{p}

I have no idea what's going on{f:, but|, but} at any rate I can't let that wreck of what used to be Kazama do as it pleases{f:.|.}
"All right. What should {f:I|I} do★"
{f:I|I} said in a panic.
"Will You Help Me, And Pray That We Defeat The Sunbararian? That Is All. Now, Here We Go☆"
{f:I|I} prayed in my heart with all my might.{p}

Just like before, {f:my|my} body began to glow again.
It seemed to be giving off light even more fiercely than before{f:.|.}
Then a dazzling light enveloped everything around.
Even in the glare, {f:I|I} didn't close my eyes.
{f:I|I} watched steadily as the Sunbararian vanished into the light.{p}

When the light died down, the Sunbararian had vanished without a trace.
The turn of events was so much that {f:I|I} could only stand there in a daze.
So in the end, Kazama really was a Sunbararian{f:.|.}
And here I thought he was just a nutcase.{p}

Wh-what... {f:I|I} only acted like that because things were moving too fast for me to keep up{f:.|.}
Every time I try to solve one problem, another one crops up, so there's nothing I can do.
And then the Sunbararian took out something like a patch and raised one hand.{p}

For an instant, the sky lit up.
It was already dark outside, so the area became as bright as day.
The light soon faded, and the darkness returned.{p}

The Sunbararian was no longer there.
...Thank goodness, it was all an illusion.
Then I happened to look down the hallway.{p}

{f:I|I} was at a loss for words.
Sunbararians, enough to fill the whole hallway, were walking toward me{f:.|.}
"It wasn't a dream{f:...|...} none of it..."
{f:I|I} could only stand there, frozen.{p}
